{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/12","id":4966063802,"node_id":"PR_kwDON1sLX88AAAABKAAeug","html_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/12","diff_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/12.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/12.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/12","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/12/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/12/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/12/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/statuses/07a28f638d2537eddf8aafdb86ef4c7bffc0da19","number":12,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Experience synced with hh.ru; a CV per position in EN/RU with 4 PDF styles; light/dark themes and 9 new positions","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #11\n\nEach item of the issue is listed below with its solution and the test that checks it. The full analysis is in the case study [`docs/case-studies/issue-11/README.md`](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-11-e1dc259e3177/docs/case-studies/issue-11/README.md). It covers the sources, the decisions, a requirement → implementation → test table, the PDF pipeline and the ATS reading-order finding.\n\n## Experience synced with hh.ru\n\n- **New jobs.**\n  - Evirma: Tech Lead, May 2026 – present.\n  - Capico LLC: Senior Software Engineer, Nov 2025 – May 2026, Tbilisi.\n  - Both have the achievements, stacks and roles from the issue.\n- **Fixed jobs.** The dates, real titles, achievements and stacks now match the issue's table:\n  - Kaiten: Development Team Lead until Nov 2025, with a team of 5 senior developers.\n  - Deep.Foundation: from Sep 2022, with all the demo projects.\n  - Abracar, ELAR, Termika, Pegas, AlpOnline and AsgardRo.\n  - ArtBridge: Web Developer.\n  - \"Lead Developer\" is no longer used for every job.\n- **LinksPlatform** stays 2010 – present. Only its 2015 – 2020 employment counts towards the total, so the total is **18 years**, as on hh.ru. It is computed, not hard-coded.\n- **Education and languages.**\n  - The \"Digital tools in the modern office\" course (2020) is added.\n  - Russian native, English C1.\n- **Russian legal names** are used in Russian: ООО «Абракар», АО «ЭЛАР», ЗАО «Термика».\n- **The data.**\n  - Jobs moved to `src/data/experience.js`, with `{ en, ru }` texts and bullets tagged by topic.\n  - Positions are in `src/data/positions.js`.\n  - Private data from hh.ru (phone, birth date, salary, email) is left out, and a test guards against it.\n\n## New positions\n\nThe old positions stay: ML/AI, DevOps, Lead, Developer and Research. The issue's nine new positions are added:\n\n- Tech Lead / Team Lead\n- CTO / Architect\n- Backend\n- Full-stack\n- .NET / C#\n- Rust\n- AI Agents / LLM\n- Trading systems\n- Data Engineer\n\nEach one has an EN/RU title and summary, plus its own jobs, skills, products and CV. All of them can be chosen on the experience page.\n\n![experience page with the CV buttons](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-11-e1dc259e3177/docs/case-studies/issue-11/screenshots/experience-cv-buttons-light.png?raw=true)\n\n## CV per position, style and language\n\n- **\"Download CV\"** on the home page and the experience page leads to `/cv/?role=…&style=…&lang=…`. That page has a preview, a position and a style picker, \"Download PDF\" and \"Print / save as PDF\".\n- **4 styles:**\n  - Classic: the reference structure.\n  - Compact: one page.\n  - Technical: stack, repository and package links.\n  - Academic: research and publications.\n- **ATS-friendly:** one column, one font, one accent color, real text, and no tables, images or SVG. Contacts are only GitHub, Telegram and the website.\n- **15 positions × 4 styles × 2 languages = 120 PDFs.** `npm run build:cv` prints them with headless Chromium after `npm run build` in the Pages workflow. They are published at `/cv/pdf/konstantin-diachenko-<position>-<style>-<lang>.pdf`.\n- **The build fails if:**\n  - a CV for a position takes more than 2 pages;\n  - a compact CV takes more than 1 page;\n  - a PDF has no text layer;\n  - any part of the CV is positioned.\n- **Page counts:** the longest tailored CV takes 1.78 pages, and every compact one takes 1 page. The full record (no position) keeps every job and takes 3 pages.\n- **Fitting 2 pages:** positions with more than 10 jobs, i.e. Developer, list the jobs that ended before 2015 in one \"Earlier experience\" line.\n- **Finding: the ATS reading order.**\n  - The first PDFs placed every job bullet after the last job in the extracted text. Chrome writes positioned elements (here, the custom `li::before` bullet) later in the PDF content stream.\n  - Plain list markers fixed it, and the build now rejects positioned parts.\n\n| Classic | Compact | Classic, Russian |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ![classic](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-11-e1dc259e3177/docs/case-studies/issue-11/screenshots/cv-classic-en.png?raw=true) | ![compact](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-11-e1dc259e3177/docs/case-studies/issue-11/screenshots/cv-compact-en.png?raw=true) | ![classic ru](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-11-e1dc259e3177/docs/case-studies/issue-11/screenshots/cv-classic-ru.png?raw=true) |\n\n| Technical | Academic |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![technical](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-11-e1dc259e3177/docs/case-studies/issue-11/screenshots/cv-technical-en.png?raw=true) | ![academic](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-11-e1dc259e3177/docs/case-studies/issue-11/screenshots/cv-academic-en.png?raw=true) |\n\n## Themes and languages\n\n- **Light and dark themes** on every page and in the CV preview.\n  - They follow `prefers-color-scheme` by default.\n  - The top-bar switch cycles system → light → dark and is remembered.\n  - The theme is applied before the first paint.\n  - Print and the PDFs are always black on white.\n- **English and Russian** for the whole site and the CV.\n  - Detected from `?lang=`, then the remembered choice, then the browser.\n  - The EN/RU switch updates the URL.\n\n| CV page, dark | CV page, light |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![dark](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-11-e1dc259e3177/docs/case-studies/issue-11/screenshots/cv-page-dark.png?raw=true) | ![light](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-11-e1dc259e3177/docs/case-studies/issue-11/screenshots/cv-page-light.png?raw=true) |\n\n| Home, Russian and light auto-detected | Experience in Russian, dark |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![home ru light](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-11-e1dc259e3177/docs/case-studies/issue-11/screenshots/home-auto-light-ru.png?raw=true) | ![experience ru dark](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-11-e1dc259e3177/docs/case-studies/issue-11/screenshots/experience-cv-buttons-ru-dark.png?raw=true) |\n\nEvery page in both themes is in [`screenshots/theme-*.png`](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/tree/issue-11-e1dc259e3177/docs/case-studies/issue-11/screenshots).\n\n## Tests\n\n341 tests pass with `npm run test:ci`:\n\n- `src/data/experience.test.js`:\n  - every job is complete (role, dates, summary, tags), and a job missing one fails the check;\n  - the hh.ru facts;\n  - the legal names;\n  - the 18 years;\n  - the positions;\n  - both languages for every text.\n- `src/cv/cv.test.jsx`:\n  - a render of every position × style × language (120 CVs) with no private data;\n  - the earlier-jobs rule;\n  - the compact, technical and academic styles;\n  - the CV page.\n- `src/cv/pdfChecks.test.js`: the page limits, page counts, text-layer and positioned-parts checks of `scripts/build-cv-pdf.mjs`.\n- `src/i18n/prefs.test.jsx`: language and theme detection, the switches and the pre-paint theme script.\n- `src/workflow.test.js`: the CV PDFs are printed into the build before the Pages artifact is uploaded.\n- `npm run build:cv` printed and checked all 120 PDFs.\n- `experiments/cv-pdf-text.py` (pypdf) extracted the text as an ATS would: 120 PDFs, 0 failures. It checks the contacts, the section headings, their order and the absence of private data.\n\n### How to try it\n\n```bash\nnpm ci\nnpm run test:ci\nnpm run build && npx playwright install chromium && npm run build:cv -- --verbose\nnpm run preview   # then open /cv/ and /experience/?role=rust\n```\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-22T10:43:14Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T21:18:31Z","closed_at":"2026-10-22T21:18:31Z","merged_at":"2026-10-22T21:18:31Z","merge_commit_sha":"955e177e9f0781d3bfc11f269cbd6680dda57c36","assignee":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":